## Journal or Meditate on:

- Where do I help others with what I have never let anyone help me with?
- What did I learn to apologize for that was never wrong?
- Whose permission am I still waiting for, and what would I do the day it arrived? Do that.
- Where were you in {{entryYear}}? What were you learning then about taking up space?

## Horoscopes for Chiron in Aries

Read your Rising Sign.

### Aries & Aries Rising

Chiron works in your 1st house, and the wound wears your name: the flinch before the first step, the identity built around being strong so nobody checks, the exhaustion of existing defensively.

Tending looks small and repetitive here: the want stated without the disclaimer, the help accepted mid-struggle instead of after, the mirror met without the inspection. The day you help someone else claim their space, and you will, the wound changes jobs. You're allowed to exist at full size while still healing. Those were never sequential. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Taurus & Taurus Rising

Chiron works in your 12th house, and the wound lives behind the scenes: the old grief that never got its season, the self-erasure so practiced it feels like personality, the tiredness with roots you haven't traced.

Tending is quiet here: the rest taken seriously, the dream tracked, the compassion practiced on your own history first. What heals in private carries the rest of the chart. You're allowed an unproductive recovery. It is the most productive thing running. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Gemini & Gemini Rising

Chiron works in your 11th house, and the wound is social: the group that never quite included you, the belonging acted out instead of felt, the friendships kept light so they can't reject anything real.

Tending looks like one honest membership: the circle where the whole personality attends, the friend told the actual news. The day a newcomer feels welcome because you remember not feeling it, the wound is working for a living. You're allowed to belong before you feel qualified. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Cancer & Cancer Rising

Chiron works in your 10th house, and the wound is public: the achievement that never silences the doubt, the authority worn like a borrowed coat, the fear of being seen failing that keeps the biggest work in the drawer.

Tending looks like scaled exposure: the small public risk survived, then the next size up. Mentoring someone through their terror of visibility will heal more of yours than any achievement has. You're allowed to be seen learning. That is what authority actually looks like. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Leo & Leo Rising

Chiron works in your 9th house, and the wound is meaning: the beliefs that failed you at a formative moment, the education interrupted or withheld, the suspicion that the big answers are for other people.

Tending looks like reclaiming the quest: the study resumed at your own pace, the faith rebuilt to your own specifications. Teaching what you had to learn the hard way is the medicine's final form. You're allowed a philosophy assembled from scars. Those hold. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Virgo & Virgo Rising

Chiron works in your 8th house, and the wound is trust: the merging that cost too much once, the debts material and emotional that taught you to keep separate accounts, the intimacy managed instead of entered.

Tending looks like graduated trust: the small vulnerable truth told and survived, the shared risk taken with a chosen person. The day you sit with someone mid-betrayal and know exactly what to say, the wound has become the skill. You're allowed to merge again. Differently, slowly, and on purpose. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Libra & Libra Rising

Chiron works in your 7th house, and the wound arrives through partners: the pattern that keeps selecting people who need you diminished, the peace kept at your own expense, the relationship as the place the existence question gets asked.

Tending looks like staying yourself in company: the preference held mid-relationship, the conflict survived without self-erasure. Helping someone else leave what you once stayed in will show you how far you've come. You're allowed a love that requires no shrinking. Accept no other kind. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Scorpio & Scorpio Rising

Chiron works in your 6th house, and the wound is daily: the body that keeps the score, the work that requires a self you have to assemble every morning, the health managed in crisis and ignored between.

Tending is routine here, literally: the appointment kept, the sustainable schedule defended, the body treated as ally instead of adversary. The day your hard-won regimen helps someone else's body, the wound is on payroll. You're allowed days that don't hurt. Build toward them. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Sagittarius & Sagittarius Rising

Chiron works in your 5th house, and the wound is joy: the creativity mocked once and shelved for years, the play that stopped being safe, the romance that asks for a visibility the old injury argues against.

Tending looks like making anyway: the art made badly on purpose, the date shown up to as yourself, the fun defended like it matters, because it does. Handing someone else their permission to create is the graduation. You're allowed unguarded delight. The critic who took it is not in the room anymore. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Capricorn & Capricorn Rising

Chiron works in your 4th house, and the wound is the foundation: the home where you learned to earn your place, the family role assigned before you could refuse it, the belonging that came with conditions.

Tending looks like rebuilding the ground: the home made unconditionally yours, the family met with boundaries and mercy in the same visit, the role resigned gently. Making your home the place where someone else finally exhales is the medicine complete. You're allowed to come from a hard place and build a soft one. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Aquarius & Aquarius Rising

Chiron works in your 3rd house, and the wound is the voice: the words dismissed early, the ideas kept in drafts, the speaking up that still costs a surcharge of nerve every single time.

Tending looks like using it anyway: the sentence said despite the tax, the writing shared before it feels ready, the conversation held at eye level. Teaching someone else to be heard is the voice's final recovery. You're allowed to take up airtime. Your words were never the problem. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

### Pisces & Pisces Rising

Chiron works in your 2nd house, and the wound is worth: the value argued from a deficit, the money that carries old shame, the enoughness that never quite arrives no matter what the account says.

Tending looks like material self-respect: the rate held through the discomfort, the belongings kept because they serve you, the worth practiced as behavior until it becomes belief. The day you talk someone off the underpricing ledge, you'll hear how healed you sound. You're allowed to cost what you cost. {{aspectHits placed per house}}

{{transitThreads}} {{yearAhead}}

